From 1000000000000000000000000000000000000470 Tue Sep  1 00:00:00 2026
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: bind Gemini CPU9 controller configuration

The production CPU9 controller profile adds its five production options to
the exact ordered configuration inputs, changing their package-derived
identity from 1e7f3047... to cda6d936....  The package provenance record and
runtime DT correctly carry the latter identity, but the MT6797 production
profile still expects the former and therefore withholds READY at proof mask
0x40000.

Bind the production profile to the exact CPU9 configuration inputs.  Keep the
fixture identity unchanged and add no CPU request, power, retry, CPU_OFF,
storage, or device action.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
index c8011a7..5cac538 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
@@ -64,8 +64,8 @@ static const u64 mt6797_a72_config_input_identity[ARM64_LATE_CPU_ID_WORDS] __ini
 };
 #else
 static const u64 mt6797_a72_config_input_identity[ARM64_LATE_CPU_ID_WORDS] __initconst = {
-	0x1e7f3047cd225aba, 0xca31d37bee725df5,
-	0x0cd0f310ff79edc5, 0x1b5838f03231b75b,
+	0xcda6d936e61122d8, 0x25a7fe7649f1b69b,
+	0x86455d6034f36a6c, 0xd562ff457bccd3d1,
 };
 #endif
 
